! BUTANONE
!**********************************************************************************************************************


! G3//MP2/aug-cc-pVDZ
! Rate constants calculated by solving the ME/RRKM equations with the MESMER software
! The pressure dependence of these two reactions is very weak !

c2h5coch3+h<=>c2h5+ch3cho              3.548E+12    -0.076    7920.7
c2h5coch3+h<=>c2h5cho+ch3              9.983E+10     0.349    9474.7


! Butanone unimolecular decomposition reactions
! Rate constants calculated by solving the ME/RRKM equations with the MESMER software
! The association ILT approach has been adopted. The rate constants of the association steps are provided as well as the 
! G3//MP2/aug-cc-pVDZ ZPE corrected 0K energies. The vibrations frequencies and the torsional PES
! of each single species (reactant and products) were calculated at the MP2/aug-cc-pVDZ level.
! The energy tranfer model adopted is <Edown> = 200 * (T/300)^0.85 1/cm
! The assocaition rate constants adopted are as follow:
! (1) c2h5co + ch3 = c2h5coch3:    1.632E+14 * T^-0.377 * exp(37.6/T)
!    the rate constant calculated by Saxena et al. (Proceedings of the Combustion Institute (2009),
!    Vol. 32, pp. 123?130) for the reaction ch3co+ch3 has been adopted as it
! (2) c2h5 + ch2co = c2h5coch3:    2.120E+14 * T^-0.401 * exp(95.3/T)
!    the rate constant calculated by Saxena has been corrected to account for the change between methyl and ethyl
!    k(c2h5+ch2co) = k(ch3+ch3co) * k(ch3+c2h5) / k (ch3+ch3)
!    the rate constants for methyl-methyl and methyl-ethyl recombination were adopted from Klippenstein et al.
!    (Physical Chemistry Chemical Physics (2006), Vol. 8, pp. 1133?1141)
! (3) ch3 + ch3coch2 = c2h5coch3:  1.358E+14 * T^-0.354 * exp(122.1/T)
!    the rate constant is assumed to be the same as the one for the reaction ch3 + c3h5-a = c4h8-1
!    the rate constant for the methyl-allyl recombination is calculated as the geometric mean of the rate constants
!    of the methyl-methyl (Klippenstein et al.) and allyl-allyl (Georgievskii et al., Physical Chemistry Chemical
!    Physics (2007), Vol. 9, pp. 4259-4268) recombination reactions
! (4) h + c2h5coch2 = c2h5coch3:  5.833E+13 * T^0.176 * exp(63/T)
!    the rate constant is assumed to be the same as the one for the reaction h + c3h5-a = c3h6
!    Harding et al., Journal of Physical Chemistry A (2007) Vol. 111, pp. 3789-3801
! (5) h + ch3chcoch3 = c2h5coch3:  2.916E+13 * T^0.176 * exp(63/T)
!    the rate constant is assumed to be the same as the one for the reaction h + c3h5-a = c3h6 but scaled
!     by a factor 0.5 to account for steric hindrance (as recommended by Harding et al.)
!    Harding et al., Journal of Physical Chemistry A (2007) Vol. 111, pp. 3789-3801
! (5) h + acetoch2 = c2h5coch3:  5.444E+13 * T^0.160
!    the rate constant is assumed to be the same as the one for the reaction h + c2h5 = c2h6
!    Harding et al., Journal of Physical Chemistry A (2005) Vol. 109, pp. 4646-4656

